  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Instead of limiting avatars in public worlds to a maximum of 2 dynamic bone collider components, I believe it would be better to set the limit based on collider affected transforms instead.  For example, I have an avatar that had 3 dynamic bone colliders, but the total collider affected transforms count was still less than the total number of dynamic bone transforms.  Due to this, I received a rejection notice for a world submission.  Under the current system, it is possible to publish an avatar with 50 dynamic bone transforms and 2 colliders that affect them all for a total of 100 collider affected transforms in a public world even though it uses more resources than one with more collider components but less affected transforms.",
